Done. From the shell, yoyo docs <missing> now exits 1 and yoyo config get <typo> exits 2. Issue #982 stays open: src/dispatch_sub.rs has 40 return Some(None) sites but only 11 places that set a failure exit code (these two included). So most shell subcommands can still print a failure and exit 0, and the grep/find no-match question is still undecided.

Exit codes:
• **`yoyo docs`:** 0 when the crate or item is found. 1 when it isn't found, when docs.rs can't be reached (the message still tells these apart) or when the crate name is invalid. Bare yoyo docs prints usage and stays 0.
• **`yoyo config get:** 2 for a key that isn't a settable key and isn't in the config file (the same misuse code as yoyo model <bad>). A real key that is just unset ("using default") stays 0, and bare config get` still exits 0 too.
• **REPL:** /docs and /config get print exactly what they did before and never exit.

What changed:
• **Docs lookup:** handle_docs_status returns the exit code alongside the output, and the shell's docs arm passes it to the existing exit_if_nonzero.
• **Config get:** `handle_config_get_status` does the same for the `config get` arm. Its core logic moved to a new `src/commands_config_get.rs`, because `commands_config.rs` went over the module-size limit (2068 lines). I split the file rather than adding it to the list of files allowed to stay oversized.
• **Existing tests:** none of the in-process dispatch tests reach the branches that now exit, so nothing had to move.

Verification: build, test, clippy and fmt all pass.
• The docs exit-code test feeds real HTTP statuses (200, 404, 410, 503, 0, and an empty 200) through the real lookup code rather than typing in the expected verdicts.
• The config tests cover: unknown key → 2 with the message unchanged, real-but-unset → 0, set key → 0.
• Sanity check on the test: forcing the docs function to always return 0 made it fail. I restored the code in the same command, and it passed again.

Running the real binary from a scratch directory, with the network up:

| command | $? |
|---|---|
| yoyo config get modle ("…did you mean model?") | 2 |
| yoyo config get model ("not set … using default") | 0 |
| yoyo docs zzz-no-such-crate-xyz ("not found on docs.rs (HTTP 404)") | 1 |
| yoyo docs serde | 0 |

docs/src/usage/commands.md now lists both codes in its existing exit-code paragraph, replacing the old "exit code is 0 in every case" line. I posted the counts and these results on #982.

